RelativeCanonicalResolution -- construction of relative canonical resolutions and Eagon-Northcott type complexes
****************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package provides functions that construct g-nodal canonical curves with a
degree k line bundle that lie on a normalized scroll. It furthermore contains
functions that compute the relative canonical resolution. The construction of
such canonical curves is based on the Macaulay2 package kGonalNodalCurves.
(see https://www.math.uni-sb.de/ag/schreyer/index.php/computeralgebra )This
package can be seen as an upgrade to the  kGonalNodalCurves  (see
https://www.math.uni-sb.de/ag/schreyer/index.php/computeralgebra ) package.


We also provide functions to compute (possibly non-minimal) free resolutions of
such curves by an iterated mapping cone construction, as described in
Schreyer's article Syzygies of Canonical Curves and Special Linear Series (see
http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2FBF01458587?LI=true ).


Construction of relative canonical resolutions
==============================================

  * *note canCurveWithFixedScroll: canCurveWithFixedScroll, -- Computes a
    g-nodal canonical curve with a degree k line bundle on a normalized scroll
  * *note curveOnScroll: curveOnScroll, -- Computes the ideal of a canonical
    curve on a normalized scroll in terms of generators of the scroll
  * *note resCurveOnScroll: resCurveOnScroll, -- Computes the relative
    canonical resolution


Iterated mapping cones and Eagon-Nortcott type complexes
========================================================

  * *note eagonNorthcottType: eagonNorthcottType, -- Computes the
    Eagon-Northcott type resolution
  * *note liftMatrixToEN: liftMatrixToEN, -- Lifts a matrix between bundles on
    the scroll to the associated Eagon-Northcott type complexes
  * *note iteratedCone: iteratedCone, -- Computes a (possibly non-minimal)
    resolution of C in P^{g-1} starting from the relative canonical resolution
    of C in P(E)

