canCurveWithFixedScroll -- Computes a g-nodal canonical curve with a degree k line bundle on a normalized scroll
****************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Ican=canCurveWithFixedScroll(g,k,n)
  * Inputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the genus of the curve
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree of the line bundle
        on C
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the integer defining the
        characteristic p ($\ge n$) of the ground field
  * Outputs:
      * ICan, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal of the canonical
        curve

Description
===========

This function computes the ideal of a g-nodal canonical curve with a degree k<g
line bundle that lies on a normalized scroll. The construction of such curves
is based on the Macaulay2 package  kGonalNodalCurves (see
http://www.math.uni-sb.de/ag/schreyer/index.php/people/researchers/75-christian
-bopp )



+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (g,k,n) = (8,5,1000);                            |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Ican = canCurveWithFixedScroll(g,k,n);           |
|                                                      |
|               ZZ                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of ----[t ..t ]                            |
|              1009  0   7                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : genus Ican, degree Ican, dim Ican                |
|                                                      |
|o3 = (8, 14, 2)                                       |
|                                                      |
|o3 : Sequence                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : betti res(Ican, DegreeLimit => 1)                |
|                                                      |
|            0  1  2  3                                |
|o4 = total: 1 15 35 21                                |
|         0: 1  .  .  .                                |
|         1: . 15 35 21                                |
|                                                      |
|o4 : BettiTally                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Phi = matrix{{t_0,t_2,t_4,t_6},{t_1,t_3,t_5,t_7}}|
|                                                      |
|o5 = | t_0 t_2 t_4 t_6 |                              |
|     | t_1 t_3 t_5 t_7 |                              |
|                                                      |
|              ZZ          2       ZZ          4       |
|o5 : Matrix (----[t ..t ])  <-- (----[t ..t ])        |
|             1009  0   7         1009  0   7          |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Iscroll = minors(2,Phi);                         |
|                                                      |
|               ZZ                                     |
|o6 : Ideal of ----[t ..t ]                            |
|              1009  0   7                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Ican + Iscroll == Ican                           |
|                                                      |
|o7 = true                                             |
