coxDegrees -- Computes the degree of a polynomial in the Cox ring corresponding to a section of a bundle on the scroll
**********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        coxDegrees(ab,e)
  * Inputs:
      * ab, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing the twist $a$ of the
        hyperplane class and $b$ of the ruling
      * e, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the type of the scroll
  * Outputs:
      * ab', a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing the bidegree in the
        Cox ring

Description
===========

This function computes integers a' and b' such that $H^0(O_{P(E)}(aH+bR))$
corresponds to basis($\{a',b'\}$,S), where S is the Cox ring of the scroll
$P(E)$.

