scrollDegrees -- Computes the degree of a section of a bundle on the scroll ring corresponding to a polynomial in the Cox ring
******************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        scrollDegrees(ab',e)
  * Inputs:
      * ab', a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing the bidegree of
        polynomial in the Cox ring
      * e, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the type of the scroll
  * Outputs:
      * ab, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing the bidegree on the
        scroll

Description
===========

This function computes integers a and b such that $H^0(O_{P(E)}(aH+bR))$
corresponds to basis($\{a',b'\}$,Rcox), where Rcox is the Cox ring of the
scroll $P(E)$.

